abstract: >-
  LaTeX source, data and verification archive, Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization (Comparator configurations checked
  with the Lean and NanoDa kernels) and interactive explainers of the manuscript "Low-discrepancy quasi-uniform
  digital sequences in every dimension" (version 1), which shows that no Halton-type, Sobol', classical Niederreiter
  or Faure sequence is quasi-uniform in dimension two and higher, and constructs, for every dimension s and every
  prime base p > 2^s, explicit quasi-uniform digital (0,s)-sequences (residue sequences). The constructions, proofs
  and Lean formalization were produced by an AI system (Anthropic Claude Opus 5.5) under the author's direction; see
  the section "Use of AI" of README.md.
